-- title:
--   Supersingular moduli places on κ(j(q),j(q^N)): existence and uniqueness
-- statement:
--   Let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic a prime $q'$, let $N \ge 1$ be an integer with $q' \nmid N$, let $E$ be an elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\kappa$ all of whose $q'$-torsion is trivial (every $P$ in `E.toAffine.Point` with $q' \cdot P = 0$ equals $0$), and let $C$ be an additive subgroup of `E.toAffine.Point` which is cyclic with `Nat.card C = N`. Inside the Laurent series field over $\kappa$, let `modularFunctionFieldC κ N` be the intermediate field generated over $\kappa$ by `jqModC κ` and its $N$-fold $q$-expansion `jqNModC κ N`, and `modularFunctionFieldFullC κ N` the one generated by `divisorExpansionsC κ N`; the first is contained in the second. Then there is exactly one place $w$ of `modularFunctionFieldC κ N` over $\kappa$ — a valuation subring containing the image of $\kappa$, different from the whole field, and a principal ideal ring — such that, first, $w$ lies in `ssPlaces q' N κ`, i.e. $w$ is rational, satisfies `IsAffineGeomPlace κ N`, and `w.evalAt (jGeomGen κ N)` lies in the set `ssJSet q' κ` of supersingular values; and second, the valuation subring of $w$ is the preimage, under the inclusion of `modularFunctionFieldC κ N` into `modularFunctionFieldFullC κ N`, of the valuation subring of `moduliPlace κ N E C`, which under the present hypotheses is the moduli place attached to the $\Gamma_0(N)$-pair consisting of $E$ together with a generator of $C$ of additive order $N$ (rather than the cusp place occurring in the degenerate branch of the definition).
--
--   This is the "values" half of the identification of the supersingular points of $X_0(N)$ in characteristic $q'$ with pairs $(E,C)$ where $E$ is supersingular and $C$ is cyclic of order $N$: the moduli place of such a pair, restricted from the full modular function field to $\kappa(j(q),j(q^N))$, is a well-defined supersingular place, and is the only one with that valuation ring. It is used in the Čerednik–Drinfeld comparison and in the constructions attaching places to Tate points at full level.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_existsUnique_mem_ssPlaces_toValuationSubring_eq_comap_moduliPlace.lean

